{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition","id":1212135,"title":"An idea for \"Powered Armor\" in Third Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-26T21:10:30-07:00","id":1212135,"title":"An idea for \"Powered Armor\" in Third Edition","content":"As a point of comparison, this is what Eric has to say about Gunshoza armor:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1211979#post1211979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current plan is that it'll be artifact armor with normal traits and Evocations. It's special because mortals can wear it and access its Evocations at great cost, but it serves as normal artifact armor for Exalted wearers.<br /> <br /> (This is, of course, subject to change; I'm only just starting to write the <i>Heirs to the Shogunate</i> outline.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So what does First Age Artifice, human-scale armor look like when it's made for the Exalted?<br /> <br /> <br /> It's <i>powered</i> armor, so it has its own Strength rating, though once you're strong enough yourself, you can actually begin to contribute something. It would also offer a Mobility bonus to movement actions.<br /> <br /> <br /> But it's <i>armor</i>, primarily, so it protects you from harm -- not as much as a warstrider, but still far more so than artifact armor usually does.<br /> <br /> Whenever you suffer levels of decisive damage, only half of those (rounded down) are applied directly to you. The rest (rounded up) are inflicted upon the armor, which has its own health levels. Depending on which has more health levels, it's possible to have the armor so badly damaged that your enemy effective strips it off of you, though it's also possible to die and leave a damaged-but-functional suit of priceless armor for your killer.<br /> <br /> Repairing the health levels of damage would work as so for a warstrider, but less expensive and demanding in some ways because of the vastly reduced scale.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, in effect, I'm suggesting a form of powered armor which is a miniature warstrider.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking such armors could exist along the entire scale from 3 to N/A, depending on how batshit crazy you make the Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:34:04-07:00","id":1212429,"title":"","content":"First Age Artefact armour, specifically designed for the Exalted, would probably be called &quot;Celestial Battle Armour.&quot; Becuase of the fact that there's no context for FAA weapons or armour (Warstriders notwithstanding) all we can do is wildly speculate. Heavy Artefact armour has 11 Soak and 10 Hardness, while Warstriders typically have 15 Soak and 10 Hardness. Do we really need more number fiddling?<br /> <br /> As for the rest of what you wrote, I also thought about the &quot;ministrider&quot; angle, which is the only context we have for FAA designed for combat, even thinking that it all might be powered by a standard hearthstone, but I never was too keen on the &quot;independent health level&quot; bit.<br /> <br /> Again, without any context, there's not much we can do but spitball, but I'll say this as a final thought. A three dot FAA would only need a Terrestrial working to create, which a DB can achieve almost trivially. In order to keep with the &quot;rare, priceless, ad barely understood angle&quot; I'd posit that Gunzosha armour would need to be 5-dots, which necessitates a Celestial Work, several Terrestrial Workings, and the actual ability to craft a 5 dot artefact, which is no easy task as a DB, as the DB Craft calculation thread can attest to.<br /> <br /> Until then, your guess is as good as anyone elses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:49:27-07:00","id":1212438,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it's going to be artifact heavy armor with a different flavoring of evocations.<br /> <br /> I'd expect the same of any other bit of powered armor.<br /> <br /> It's not better. It's different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:57:50-07:00","id":1212444,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of armor that has its own health levels and takes half your injuries for you.<br /> <br /> A miniature warstrider seems like a perfectly acceptable idea for First Age Artifice armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:03:25-07:00","id":1212450,"title":"","content":"It'd certainly justify spending XP on a suit of armour for yourself, and the fact that its needs periodic repairs, but I just don't feel it to be too interesting. Not that I can come up with anything better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:07:32-07:00","id":1212455,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I'm remembering this correctly, but to my mind the Devs have said that FAA stuff is not to be simply mechanically better than non-FAA stuff, but that would allow access to free powers and some baseline Evocations.<br /> <br /> So a FAA Heavy armor would be mechanically the same as an Artifact Armor, but could let you say, fly at will and come with some free unlocked mobility Evocations.<br /> <br /> Or maybe it could make you immune the elements and sustain your bodily functions indefinitely without sleep.<br /> <br /> Or any other shit that if reproduced in mass would distort the setting.<br /> <br /> But not straight up better like what you mentioned. Could be that I'm mistaken though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:10:14-07:00","id":1212456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VioletDreamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212438#post1212438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it's going to be artifact heavy armor with a different flavoring of evocations.<br /> <br /> I'd expect the same of any other bit of powered armor.<br /> <br /> It's not better. It's different.</div> </div> </div> </div>If different doesn\u2019t mean better for First Age Artifice armor, then there\u2019s no point in making it.<br /> <br /> Gunshoza armor is better in that mortals can use it.<br /> <br /> Celestial Battle Armor intended for Exalted should offer something that regular artifact armor doesn\u2019t.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:17:53-07:00","id":1212462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212456#post1212456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If different doesn\u2019t mean better for First Age Artifice armor, then there\u2019s no point in making it.<br /> <br /> Gunshoza armor is better in that mortals can use it.<br /> <br /> Celestial Battle Armor intended for Exalted should offer something that regular artifact armor doesn\u2019t.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been discussed by Devs, don't remember if the current or previous ones, but that was not their approach. FAA is not to be a vertical widget on the power scale, but an horizontal broadening of what can be achieved with an Artifact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T15:51:58-07:00","id":1212474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212462#post1212462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has been discussed by Devs, don't remember if the current or previous ones, but that was not their approach. FAA is not to be a vertical widget on the power scale, but an horizontal broadening of what can be achieved with an Artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you feel my idea is inappropriate?<br /> <br /> Probably, they\u2019re talking about things like the power of individual Evocations. Like giving a five-dot sword something stronger than Volcano Cutter\u2019s pinnacle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:27:05-07:00","id":1212486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212474#post1212474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you feel my idea is inappropriate?<br /> <br /> Probably, they\u2019re talking about things like the power of individual Evocations. Like giving a five-dot sword something stronger than Volcano Cutter\u2019s pinnacle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not inherently, no. After all there are many other effects that grant health levels.<br /> <br /> Though I would make the additional health levels a function of a specific suit of FAA Armor. Not a function of all FAA Armor.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T16:40:31-07:00","id":1212492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212486#post1212486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make the additional health levels a function of a specific suit of FAA Armor. Not a function of all FAA Armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it\u2019s not universal to all FFA armor. It clearly isn\u2019t the plan for Gunshoza armor, and the idea really won\u2019t work for armor that isn\u2019t full-body covering.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea might still work with light armor, because that gets you something like Terry McGinnis\u2019 armor in Batman Beyond.<br /> <br /> But there are other possibilities for FFA armor or clothing besides acting like a miniature mecha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T19:15:09-07:00","id":1212517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212492#post1212492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it\u2019s not universal to all FFA armor. It clearly isn\u2019t the plan for Gunshoza armor, and the idea really won\u2019t work for armor that isn\u2019t full-body covering.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea might still work with light armor, because that gets you something like Terry McGinnis\u2019 armor in Batman Beyond.<br /> <br /> But there are other possibilities for FFA armor or clothing besides acting like a miniature mecha.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just making clear that I don't believe that Celestial Battle Armor is a baseline denomination, but one of many interpretations of Powerarmor for Exalted users.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T00:52:13-07:00","id":1212556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition#post1212135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <i>powered</i> armor, so it has its own Strength rating, though once you're strong enough yourself, you can actually begin to contribute something. It would also offer a Mobility bonus to movement actions.<br /> <br /> But it's <i>armor</i>, primarily, so it protects you from harm -- not as much as a warstrider, but still far more so than artifact armor usually does.<br /> <br /> Whenever you suffer levels of decisive damage, only half of those (rounded down) are applied directly to you. The rest (rounded up) are inflicted upon the armor, which has its own health levels. Depending on which has more health levels, it's possible to have the armor so badly damaged that your enemy effective strips it off of you, though it's also possible to die and leave a damaged-but-functional suit of priceless armor for your killer.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking such armors could exist along the entire scale from 3 to N/A, depending on how batshit crazy you make the Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Free Strength dots <i>plus </i>free dice on movement actions <i>plus </i>the equivalent of free Ox-Body purchases is a hell of a lot more upfront power than most 3 or 4-dots give you, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T03:01:13-07:00","id":1212574,"title":"","content":"isnt this edition trying to get away from this kind of thing. Couldnt these effects be done more through evocatons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:20:35-07:00","id":1212603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212556#post1212556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Free Strength dots <i>plus </i>free dice on movement actions <i>plus </i>the equivalent of free Ox-Body purchases is a hell of a lot more upfront power than most 3 or 4-dots give you, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>@Nihilum rightly points out that Three-Dots is too low, as Dragon-Blooded shouldn't be able to construct armor like this. The lowest rating should be Four-Dots, which requires Celestial workings.<br /> <br /> It's possible that Celestial Battle Armor should only be Five-Dot and NA, as per warstriders, with the balance being that the armor can be used anywhere, doesn't suffer the same stealth penalties, and perhaps might be able to go longer without maintenance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212574#post1212574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">isnt this edition trying to get away from this kind of thing. Couldnt these effects be done more through evocatons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Warstriders need Evocations for any of their basic advantages?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:43:52-07:00","id":1212633,"title":"","content":"Warstrider's basic advantages are all consequences of being <i>thirty feet tall</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T08:14:38-07:00","id":1212667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212633#post1212633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Warstrider's basic advantages are all consequences of being <i>thirty feet tall</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things larger than warstriders don't get devastating actions.<br /> <br /> Things smaller than warstriders can have lower Strength ratings and fewer health levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T17:47:42-07:00","id":1212856,"title":"","content":"First Age Artifacts are pretty much just there to serve as a catch for stuff that would be disruptive to the setting.<br /> <br /> Ox-body as a free first evocation works just fine, lots of artifacts offer a free first evocation. That said you'll want to gate your muscle actuators or whatever. Strength bonus and movement bonus with first charm purchased, or with a rocketed hearth stone might work. From there wrist mounted rocket launchers, shoulder miniguns, and jetpacks as evocations to your hearts content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T17:59:25-07:00","id":1212859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1212856#post1212856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Age Artifacts are pretty much just there to serve as a catch for stuff that would be disruptive to the setting.<br /> <br /> Ox-body as a free first evocation works just fine, lots of artifacts offer a free first evocation. That said you'll want to gate your muscle actuators or whatever. Strength bonus and movement bonus with first charm purchased, or with a rocketed hearth stone might work. From there wrist mounted rocket launchers, shoulder miniguns, and jetpacks as evocations to your hearts content.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y\u2019all probably have a point.<br /> <br /> First Age Artifice is for... lateral? Abilities. Gunshoza armor is more of a logistical miracle in that mortals can use it without making it any more powerful for Exalted.<br /> <br /> The strength and mobility advantages can be Evocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T08:47:36-07:00","id":1213073,"title":"","content":"To me, power armor should be \u201cpowered\u201d - not so much by your own magic, but by something in the armor. As such, it should have a power source - like a major Hearthstone. And in my mind, if the armor is powered by the power source, it should automatically have all of the (assuredly flashy) evocations unlocked. I\u2019m thinking strength, speed, flight, energy weapons, maybe an energy sword, etc. - all tuned to whatever the point of the armor has been designed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Host of <a href=\"http://www.fivepoles.com/podcast/\" target=\"_blank\">The Deliberative Podcast</a><br /> Host of <a href=\"https://tca.edennian.com\" target=\"_blank\">Trinity Continuum Airwaves</a><br /> Original Creator of the complete <a href=\"https://www.fantasygrounds.com/forums/showthread.php?9238-Rules-Lite-New-World-of-Darkness&amp;highlight=\" target=\"_blank\">nWoD conversion of Fantasy Grounds 2</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12730-pneumapilot","name":"PneumaPilot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12730_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"149"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T09:07:37-07:00","id":1213083,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, the current plan for gunzosha armor (and other &quot;powered armor&quot; artifacts) is to use the same paradigm as the combat modules on the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation. Evocations will represent mastering specific armor components \u2014 a sense-enhancing visor, exomuscular amplifiers, or the like. This is meant to provide the flavor of powered armor while avoiding intractable game-balance issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:13:10-07:00","id":1213098,"title":"","content":"Definitely, an Ironman Armor needs an Arc Reactor of some variety, but that doesn't necessitate that Tony Stark has adapted to the needs of his suit enough to properly employ its musculature. Heck, we had a long sequence where he learns the Evocations for flying with it before he ever takes it out into combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:20:27-07:00","id":1213101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1213083#post1213083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, the current plan for gunzosha armor (and other &quot;powered armor&quot; artifacts) is to use the same paradigm as the combat modules on the Cathedral of Sublime Annihilation. Evocations will represent mastering specific armor components \u2014 a sense-enhancing visor, exomuscular amplifiers, or the like. This is meant to provide the flavor of powered armor while avoiding intractable game-balance issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a very interesting way of handling it. Will it have any passive bonuses that you get for simply attuning to it? Will you need a Hearthstone to power it?<br /> <br /> Is there any chance that Exalt specific power armour, something like Celestial Battle Armour would exist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:25:04-07:00","id":1213106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nilihum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1213101#post1213101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems like a very interesting way of handling it. Will it have any passive bonuses that you get for simply attuning to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, just like all artifacts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Will you need a Hearthstone to power it? </div> </div> </div>The original gunzosha armor in First Edition didn't need 'em, and I don't think it'd make sense to add that in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any chance that Exalt specific power armour, something like Celestial Battle Armour would exist? </div> </div> </div>It's not impossible!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T10:45:44-07:00","id":1213118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1213106#post1213106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, just like all artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more in lines with the added strength that Warstriders grant or the various flight based passives you get when attuned to Ascendant Nova Phoenix as opposed to &quot;+1 Evocation on attunement&quot; or &quot;+1 Resolve&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2388-nilihum","name":"Nilihum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2388_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:18:03-07:00","id":1213163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nilihum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1212135-an-idea-for-powered-armor-in-third-edition?p=1213118#post1213118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking more in lines with the added strength that Warstriders grant or the various flight based passives you get when attuned to Ascendant Nova Phoenix as opposed to &quot;+1 Evocation on attunement&quot; or &quot;+1 Resolve&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as extensive as the bonuses warstriders pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:32:07-07:00","id":1213622,"title":"","content":"After my ST explained Gunzosha armor to me, I honestly just thought that it was heavy artifact armor suit a mortal could wield. The working that go into its construction are what allow a mortal to utilize it even at the great cost they pay to use it. The evocations and stuff that Vance and Minton mentioned make perfect sense and a great way to offer the variety of customization without the potential hideous power balance issues of it. Thinking of it from my point of view how amazing would a exo armor suit that mortals can use be? Something that gives a mortal a chance to fight at exalt level skill is pretty amazing as is.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to comment on the idea of the Celestial Battle Armor idea. I think it could be fun to design a suit for a char to run around in. I admit though I think I would struggle with how to make it fill the rather small niche between artifact 5 armor and a warstrider.<br /> <br /> Any case thanks for a interesting thread read so far <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}